---
source: crates/cli/tests/native.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
Fast, native developer tools

Usage: tw <COMMAND>

Commands:
  jq           Query and transform JSON, YAML, TOML, XML and CSV, as jq 1.8 does
  json         Format, minify and validate JSON, written as jq . writes it
  convert      Between JSON, YAML 1.2, TOML, CSV and XML
  base64       Encode and decode Base64 (RFC 4648)
  base32       Encode and decode Base32 (RFC 4648), as GNU base32 does
  hex          Bytes as hexadecimal and back, as xxd -p and xxd -r -p
  url          Percent-encode, decode and take URLs apart (RFC 3986, WHATWG)
  jwt          Decode, verify and create JSON Web Tokens (RFC 7519)
  cert         What an X.509 certificate or chain says: names, validity, key, fingerprints
  md5sum       MD5 checksums of files, or check them
  sha1sum      SHA-1 checksums of files, or check them
  sha256sum    SHA-256 checksums of files, or check them
  sha512sum    SHA-512 checksums of files, or check them
  b2sum        BLAKE2b checksums of files, or check them
  b3sum        BLAKE3 checksums of files, or check them, as b3sum does
  hmac         HMAC of the input with a secret key, as openssl dgst -hmac
  bcrypt       Hash a password with bcrypt, or check one against its hash
  argon2       Hash a password with Argon2id, Argon2i or Argon2d, as the argon2 command does
  random       Passwords, tokens and bytes from the system's secure generator
  uuid         Generate UUIDs, or read what one holds (RFC 9562)
  ulid         Generate and read ULIDs: IDs that sort by time, as UUIDs too
  time         Unix timestamps, ISO 8601 and RFC dates, in any time zone
  cron         What a cron expression means, and when it runs next
  regex        Test a pattern, see its matches and groups, replace with it
  diff         Compare two files line by line, as GNU diff does
  ipcalc       An address and prefix's network, netmask, broadcast, hosts and address space
  case         One name in every case code uses: camelCase, snake_case, kebab-case…
  base         A number in binary, octal, decimal, hex or any base from 2 to 36
  list         List every tool
  completions  Print shell completions
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
